target/
# The whole directory, not just cache/ — this is for git-status hygiene only (kndo's own
# `.kndo/.gitignore`, written by `cache::FactsCache::open`, is what actually keeps `cache/`
# out of `git add -A`; discovery.rs excludes `.kndo/` from analysis unconditionally,
# independent of this file, since a project's first-ever run predates any gitignore entry).
.kndo/

# Conformance fixture corpora are NOT excluded here — they are checked into git, and this file
# governs `git add` for untracked files, so an entry here silently skips a newly added fixture
# (green locally, absent from CI). The exclusion they do need is from kndo's own analysis, and
# that lives in `.ignore`, which the `ignore` crate reads and git does not.
docs/book/

# Local coverage output (CONTRIBUTING.md "Coverage") — kndo ingests lcov.info from the
# repo root or coverage/ at check time; the report itself is a build artifact.
lcov.info
coverage/
# …except a conformance fixture's captured report: its pin depends on it, so it IS
# repo content — exactly the "green locally, absent from CI" trap the note above names,
# which three fixtures fell into before this line existed.
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/**/coverage/
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/**/lcov.info

# `cargo xtask package` output — release artifacts are built by CI, never committed.
dist/
# …except a fixture's own tree: `src-layout-roots` names its distribution `dist`,
# and this line ate the two modules its pinned report is OF — the same trap the
# coverage note above names, one directory further down.
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/**/dist/

# Claude Code's own tooling state (session worktrees for parallel-agent workflows, etc.) —
# local to the machine running the session, never repo content. `skills/` is the one exception:
# a project-local skill is repo content, meant to travel with a clone the same way CLAUDE.md
# does, not to stay behind on the machine that authored it.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
